Documentation
Objectives
The repository should include a README.md.

The README should contain:

Project name
Short description of the app
Installation/setup instructions
Instructions for running the app
Instructions for running the tests and generating the coverage report
List of main features
Any known limitations
Names of all team members
The repository should include a simple design document at docs/design.md that includes (at least):

System architecture: major classes/modules, their responsibilities and interactions
User interface design: mock-ups, expected interactions/workflows
Explanations for important design decisions or tradeoffs
Assessment
Documentation will be assessed based on whether:

It is present, accurate, and up-to-date
The grader can test and run the app using only the instructions provided in the README
Lightweight Planning Artifacts
Backlog
Objectives
The project should maintain a small backlog of work items at docs/backlog.md

The backlog should include:

User stories or feature ideas
Task breakdowns for implementation
Status of work items, such as:
To Do
In Progress
Done
Assessment
The backlog will be assessed based on whether:

It exists
It was updated in timely manner during the project
It reflects the implemented work
It shows reasonable planning
Planning
Objectives
The team should hold a planning discussion near the start of the project and document the discussion in docs/planning.md .

The planning discussion should address:

What app the team will build
Which features are essential and which are optional
How the team will collaborate on work (individual vs. pair programming)
What “done” means for the project and for individual features/stories
Assessment
The planning discussion will be assessed based on whether the documentation:

Is present
Shows meaningful planning
Is specific to the project and consistent with the actual development history
Retrospective
Objectives
The team should hold a retrospective discussion near the end of the project and document the discussion in docs/retrospective.md.

The retrospective discussion should address:

What went well
What was difficult
What the pair would improve next time
Whether the final app met the original goal
Assessment
The retrospective discussion will be assessed based on whether the documentation:

Is present
Shows meaningful reflection
Is specific to the project and consistent with the actual development history
